    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nThe intro logo looks misaligned with Cascadia Code and Consolas. These are the default monospaced fonts on Windows / WSL so it probably affects a good number of people.\n\nCascadia Code:\n<img width=\"972\" height=\"333\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/259702c5-04a5-40cd-b651-955f2446bf94\" />\n\nConsolas:\n<img width=\"752\" height=\"312\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5749e343-eee4-4eb8-9350-6e5309e8c053\" />\n\nExamples using font size: 22. But reproduces on all font sizes.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Install NVIM v0.13.0-dev-1061+g01c4d37959 nightly release\n2. Run nvim-linux-x86_64.appimage with font set to Cascadia Code or Consolas  in WSL.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nMaybe an option to disable the logo for people using fonts that don't support it.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1061+g01c4d37959\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo N/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nWindows 11 (Build 26200) (WSL)\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nWindows Terminal\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nappimage",
